IMPORT prelude

-- Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth) -- the parts the Western Australian lives ask about: who is a consumer (Sch 2 s 3),
-- the guarantee of acceptable quality (Sch 2 s 54), the remedies against a supplier of goods and who chooses them (Sch 2 ss 259,
-- 260, 261, 262, 263(4)), guarantees that cannot be contracted out of and the business-to-business limitation that may be
-- (Sch 2 ss 64, 64A), unfair terms in consumer and small business contracts (Sch 2 ss 23, 24, 26, 27), misleading or deceptive
-- conduct (Sch 2 s 18), harassment and coercion (Sch 2 s 50), the Schedule's reach as Commonwealth law (ss 131, 131A), and when an
-- acquisition must be notified to the ACCC under the new Part IVA (ss 51ABB, 51ABD, 51ABE(2), 51ABJ, 51ABO, 51ABP, 51ABS, 51ABT,
-- 51ABV(6)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 166, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 76, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00389, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00109.txt. The deposit's metadata warns that a version in
-- force from 16 September 2026 had no registered compilation when it was fetched, so later amendments may be missing.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0018 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 5 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c070 (2032-05-20, a new laptop fails in month three and the retailer repairs it:
-- what guarantees apply, and who chooses the remedy?); Jake k064 (2037-02-06, debts of $41,000 and collectors call: what may a
-- collector do?); Daniel d045 (2031-07-10, Jarrah's standard software terms: is a liability cap an unfair term in a small-business
-- contract, and are the consumer guarantees excluded?), d056 (2039-02-11, a competitor trades as JARRA: is it misleading
-- conduct?) and d065 (2043-06-15, Jarrah acquires Formly Pty Ltd: must the acquisition be notified to the ACCC?). SCOPED to the
-- provisions those events name, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Everything else in a four-volume Act: Part IV (restrictive trade practices), the rest of Part IVA (notification
-- procedure, ACCC determinations, phase 2, public benefit, Tribunal review) and Division 1A of Part IV (consequences of not
-- notifying); the other guarantees (ss 51-53, 55-63) except as s 259 and s 64A name them; services remedies (ss 267-270);
-- manufacturers' liability (Part 5-4 Div 2); the s 25 examples of unfair terms; s 28 and s 28A exclusions (an INPUT); pecuniary
-- penalties (s 224) and their amounts; the ACCC/ASIC debt collection guideline, which k064 names but which is not in the Act; the
-- ACL as a law of Western Australia (applied by the Fair Trading Act 2010 (WA), not deposited). The NOTIFICATION THRESHOLDS and
-- notifiable classes are made by the Minister by legislative instrument (ss 51ABP, 51ABQ, 51ABRA, 51ABRB, 51ABS(6)) and are not
-- in the Act: whether an acquisition meets them is an INPUT. A "greater amount" prescribed for the $40,000 consumer threshold
-- (s 3(1)(a)(ii)) is an INPUT. "Financial services" and "financial products" (ASIC Act and Corporations Act meanings), "control"
-- (Corporations Act s 50AA) and "voting power" are INPUTS. The evaluative judgements (acceptable quality, major failure, unfair,
-- misleading, undue harassment) are INPUTS: the Act names the test; a court applies it.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not available in this
-- session; the finished naive encodings in subjects/sg were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Competition and Consumer Act 2010 -- the Australian Consumer Law and merger notification`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `ss 131, 131A -- the Schedule as a law of the Commonwealth`

-- s 131(1): "Schedule 2 applies as a law of the Commonwealth to the conduct of corporations".
-- s 131A(1): "Despite section 131, this Division does not apply ... to the supply, or possible supply, of services that are
-- financial services, or of financial products" (save Division 3A of Part 3-2, Division 3A of Part 4-2 and Part 5-5).
-- (2)(a): "Part 2-1 of Schedule 2 [s 18] ... do[es] not apply to conduct engaged in in relation to financial services";
-- (2)(b): Part 2-3 (unfair terms) does not apply to contracts that are financial products or for financial services.
-- Naive simplification: "corporation" is an input flag, and the extensions in ss 5, 6 and 131(2) are not modelled.
GIVEN `the trader is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `it concerns financial services or financial products` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule applies as Commonwealth law` IF
    `the trader is a corporation` AND (NOT `it concerns financial services or financial products`)

§§ `Sch 2 s 3 -- acquiring as a consumer`

-- s 3(1): "A person is taken to have acquired particular goods as a consumer if, and only if: (a) the amount paid or payable for
-- the goods ... did not exceed: (i) $40,000; or (ii) if a greater amount is prescribed ... that greater amount; or (b) the goods
-- were of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption; or (c) the goods consisted of a
-- vehicle or trailer acquired for use principally in the transport of goods on public roads."
-- (2): "However, subsection (1) does not apply if the person acquired the goods ... (a) ... for the purpose of re-supply; or (b)
-- for the purpose of using them up or transforming them, in trade or commerce" in production, manufacture or repair.
-- (3): services likewise, by (a) the $40,000 test or (b) the personal kind -- with no re-supply exception.
-- s 2: "goods includes ... (e) computer software".
-- (10): a person alleged to be a consumer "is presumed, unless the contrary is established" to be one.
DECLARE Acquisition HAS
    `is of goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount paid or payable` IS A NUMBER
    `greater amount prescribed` IS A NUMBER
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a vehicle or trailer for transporting goods on public roads` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired for re-supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired to use up or transform in production or repair` IS A BOOLEAN

`the consumer threshold in the Act` MEANS 40000

GIVEN `the acquisition` IS AN Acquisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was acquired as a consumer` IF
    IF `the acquisition`'s `is of goods`
    THEN (    `the acquisition`'s `amount paid or payable` AT MOST `the larger of` `the consumer threshold in the Act` (`the acquisition`'s `greater amount prescribed`)
          OR  `the acquisition`'s `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use`
          OR  `the acquisition`'s `a vehicle or trailer for transporting goods on public roads`)
         AND (NOT `the acquisition`'s `acquired for re-supply`)
         AND (NOT `the acquisition`'s `acquired to use up or transform in production or repair`)
    ELSE     `the acquisition`'s `amount paid or payable` AT MOST `the larger of` `the consumer threshold in the Act` (`the acquisition`'s `greater amount prescribed`)
          OR `the acquisition`'s `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use`

§§ `Sch 2 s 54 -- the guarantee of acceptable quality`

-- s 54(1): "If: (a) a person supplies, in trade or commerce, goods to a consumer; and (b) the supply does not occur by way of
-- sale by auction; there is a guarantee that the goods are of acceptable quality."
-- (2): acceptable quality means as "(a) fit for all the purposes for which goods of that kind are commonly supplied; and (b)
-- acceptable in appearance and finish; and (c) free from defects; and (d) safe; and (e) durable; as a reasonable consumer fully
-- acquainted with the state and condition of the goods (including any hidden defects ...) would regard as acceptable", having
-- regard to nature, price, packaging statements, representations and other circumstances (3).
-- (4): taken to be of acceptable quality if "the only reason or reasons why they are not ... were specifically drawn to the
-- consumer's attention before the consumer agreed to the supply".
-- (6): they do not fail if "(a) the consumer ... causes them to become of unacceptable quality, or fails to take reasonable steps
-- to prevent them from becoming of unacceptable quality; AND (b) they are damaged by abnormal use." -- both limbs, as written.
-- (7): nor if the consumer examined them and "the examination ought reasonably to have revealed" the problem.
GIVEN `supplied in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN, `the buyer is a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN, `sold by auction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guarantee of acceptable quality applies` IF
    `supplied in trade or commerce` AND `the buyer is a consumer` AND (NOT `sold by auction`)

DECLARE `State of the goods` HAS
    `a reasonable consumer would regard them as fit, finished, free from defects, safe and durable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only reasons were drawn to the consumer's attention before the supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer caused it or failed to take reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damaged by abnormal use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pre-supply examination ought to have revealed it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the goods` IS A `State of the goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are of acceptable quality` IF
        `the goods`'s `a reasonable consumer would regard them as fit, finished, free from defects, safe and durable`
    OR  `the goods`'s `the only reasons were drawn to the consumer's attention before the supply`
    OR  (`the goods`'s `the consumer caused it or failed to take reasonable steps` AND `the goods`'s `damaged by abnormal use`)
    OR  `the goods`'s `a pre-supply examination ought to have revealed it`

§§ `Sch 2 ss 259-263 -- remedies against the supplier, and who chooses`

-- s 259(1): a consumer may act if a supplier supplies goods in trade or commerce and a guarantee in Subdivision A (other than
-- ss 58 and 59(1)) "is not complied with".
-- (2): "If the failure ... can be remedied and is not a major failure: (a) the consumer may require the supplier to remedy the
-- failure within a reasonable time; or (b) if ... the supplier refuses or fails to comply ... the consumer may: (i) otherwise
-- have the failure remedied and ... recover all reasonable costs ...; or (ii) subject to section 262, notify the supplier that
-- the consumer rejects the goods".
-- (3): "If the failure ... cannot be remedied or is a major failure, the consumer may: (a) subject to section 262, ... reject[]
-- the goods ...; or (b) ... recover compensation for any reduction in the value of the goods below the price paid".
-- (4): damages for reasonably foreseeable loss; (5): not if the failure "occurred only because of a cause independent of human
-- control that occurred after the goods left the control of the supplier".
-- s 261: when required to remedy, "the supplier may comply ... (b) ... by repairing the goods; or (c) by replacing the goods
-- ...; or (d) by refunding". THE SUPPLIER picks.
-- s 263(4): on rejection, "The supplier must, IN ACCORDANCE WITH AN ELECTION MADE BY THE CONSUMER: (a) refund ...; or (b)
-- replace the rejected goods". THE CONSUMER picks.
-- s 260(1): a major failure if "(a) the goods would not have been acquired by a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the
-- nature and extent of the failure; or (b) [significant departure from description or sample]; or (c) ... substantially unfit
-- for a purpose for which goods of the same kind are commonly supplied and they cannot, easily and within a reasonable time, be
-- remedied ...; or (d) [the same for a disclosed purpose]; or (e) the goods are not of acceptable quality because they are
-- unsafe." (2): also where two or more failures, "taken as a whole", would have deterred a reasonable consumer.
-- s 262(1): no rejection if "(a) the rejection period ... has ended; or (b) the goods have been lost, destroyed or disposed of
-- ...; or (c) ... damaged after being delivered ... for reasons not related to their state or condition at the time of supply;
-- or (d) ... attached to, or incorporated in" other property and cannot be detached without damage.
DECLARE Failure HAS
    `a guarantee was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable consumer would not have bought them knowing of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `departs significantly from description or sample` IS A BOOLEAN
    `substantially unfit for a common or disclosed purpose and not easily remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unsafe` IS A BOOLEAN
    `several failures taken together would have deterred a reasonable consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `can be remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer required a remedy and the supplier failed within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rejection period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lost, destroyed, disposed of, damaged after delivery or attached` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss was reasonably foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused only by something independent of human control after leaving the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a major failure` IF
        `the failure`'s `a reasonable consumer would not have bought them knowing of it`
    OR  `the failure`'s `departs significantly from description or sample`
    OR  `the failure`'s `substantially unfit for a common or disclosed purpose and not easily remedied`
    OR  `the failure`'s `unsafe`
    OR  `the failure`'s `several failures taken together would have deterred a reasonable consumer`

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may only require a remedy, for now` IF
        `the failure`'s `a guarantee was not complied with`
    AND `the failure`'s `can be remedied`
    AND (NOT `it is a major failure` `the failure`)
    AND (NOT `the failure`'s `the consumer required a remedy and the supplier failed within a reasonable time`)

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may reject the goods` IF
        `the failure`'s `a guarantee was not complied with`
    AND (    `it is a major failure` `the failure`
         OR  (NOT `the failure`'s `can be remedied`)
         OR  `the failure`'s `the consumer required a remedy and the supplier failed within a reasonable time`)
    AND (NOT `the failure`'s `the rejection period has ended`)
    AND (NOT `the failure`'s `lost, destroyed, disposed of, damaged after delivery or attached`)

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may recover compensation for the drop in value` IF
        `the failure`'s `a guarantee was not complied with`
    AND (`it is a major failure` `the failure` OR (NOT `the failure`'s `can be remedied`))

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may recover damages for consequential loss` IF
        `the failure`'s `a guarantee was not complied with`
    AND `the failure`'s `the loss was reasonably foreseeable`
    AND (NOT `the failure`'s `caused only by something independent of human control after leaving the supplier`)

DECLARE Chooser IS ONE OF
    `the supplier chooses repair, replacement or refund`
    `the consumer chooses`
    `no remedy under s 259`

-- Who chooses the remedy (the question c070 asks): in a remediable, non-major failure the consumer may only require a remedy and
-- s 261 lets the supplier choose its form; once the failure is major or cannot be remedied, or the supplier has failed to remedy
-- it, the consumer chooses -- between rejection (and then refund or replacement, s 263(4)), compensation, or a remedy elsewhere.
GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A Chooser
`who chooses the remedy` MEANS
    IF NOT `the failure`'s `a guarantee was not complied with`
    THEN `no remedy under s 259`
    ELSE IF `the consumer may only require a remedy, for now` `the failure`
         THEN `the supplier chooses repair, replacement or refund`
         ELSE `the consumer chooses`

§§ `Sch 2 ss 64, 64A -- the guarantees cannot be excluded, save one limitation`

-- s 64(1): "A term of a contract ... is void to the extent that the term purports to exclude, restrict or modify, or has the
-- effect of excluding, restricting or modifying: (a) the application of all or any of the provisions of this Division; or (b)
-- the exercise of a right conferred by such a provision; or (c) any liability of a person for a failure to comply with a
-- guarantee". (2): a term does so only "if the term does so expressly or is inconsistent with the provision".
-- s 64A(1): for goods "other than goods of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use", a term is not
-- void "merely because the term limits the person's liability for failure to comply with a guarantee (other than a guarantee
-- under section 51, 52 or 53) to ... (a) the replacement of the goods ...; (b) the repair of the goods; (c) the payment of the
-- cost of replacing the goods ...; (d) the payment of the cost of having the goods repaired."
-- (2): for non-household services, limiting liability to "(a) the supplying of the services again; or (b) the payment of the
-- cost of having the services supplied again."
-- (3): s 64A does not apply "if the person to whom the goods or services were supplied establishes that it is not fair or
-- reasonable for the person who supplied the goods or services to rely on that term".
-- The guarantees only exist where the customer acquired "as a consumer" (s 3) -- which a business customer paying $40,000 or
-- less does, whatever the kind of goods or services.
DECLARE Term HAS
    `expressly or inconsistently excludes, restricts or modifies the guarantees or liability for them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supply is of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limits liability only to the s 64A remedies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `touches the title guarantees in ss 51 to 53` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the customer establishes reliance on it is not fair or reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the term` IS A Term
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64A saves the term` IF
        (NOT `the term`'s `the supply is of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use`)
    AND `the term`'s `limits liability only to the s 64A remedies`
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `touches the title guarantees in ss 51 to 53`)
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `the customer establishes reliance on it is not fair or reasonable`)

GIVEN `the term` IS A Term, `the customer acquired as a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is void under s 64` IF
        `the customer acquired as a consumer`
    AND `the term`'s `expressly or inconsistently excludes, restricts or modifies the guarantees or liability for them`
    AND (NOT `s 64A saves the term` `the term`)

§§ `Sch 2 ss 23, 24, 26, 27 -- unfair terms in consumer and small business contracts`

-- s 23(1): "A term of a consumer contract or small business contract is void if: (a) the term is unfair; and (b) the contract is
-- a standard form contract." (2A): a person contravenes if it makes such a contract and "proposed the unfair term"; (2C): or
-- "applies or relies on" one. (2B): a separate contravention "in respect of each term".
-- (3): "A consumer contract is a contract for ... a supply of goods or services ... to an individual whose acquisition ... is
-- wholly or predominantly for personal, domestic or household use or consumption."
-- (4): "A contract is a small business contract if: (a) the contract is for a supply of goods or services, or a sale or grant of
-- an interest in land; and (b) AT LEAST ONE PARTY to the contract satisfies either or both of the following conditions: (i) the
-- party makes the contract in the course of carrying on a business and at a time when the party employs fewer than 100 persons;
-- (ii) the party's turnover ... for the party's last income year ... is less than $10,000,000." (5): casuals count only if
-- regular and systematic; part-timers as a fraction of a full-time equivalent -- the head count is an INPUT.
-- s 24(1): unfair if "(a) it would cause a significant imbalance ...; and (b) it is not reasonably necessary in order to protect
-- the legitimate interests of the party who would be advantaged by the term; and (c) it would cause detriment". (4): (b) "is
-- presumed ... unless that party proves otherwise".
-- s 26(1): s 23 does not apply to a term to the extent it "(a) ... defines the main subject matter ...; (b) ... sets the upfront
-- price ...; (c) ... is required, or expressly permitted, by a law" (and (d), (e)).
-- s 27(1): a contract alleged to be standard form "is presumed to be a standard form contract unless another party ... proves
-- otherwise".
-- s 28, s 28A and s 131A(2)(b) exclusions are one INPUT flag.
DECLARE Party HAS
    `contracts in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `persons employed, counted under s 23(5)` IS A NUMBER
    `turnover for its last income year` IS A NUMBER

`the small business head count` MEANS 100
`the small business turnover` MEANS 10000000

GIVEN `the party` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party is small for s 23(4)` IF
        (`the party`'s `contracts in the course of a business` AND `the party`'s `persons employed, counted under s 23(5)` LESS THAN `the small business head count`)
    OR  `the party`'s `turnover for its last income year` LESS THAN `the small business turnover`

GIVEN `the supplier party` IS A Party, `the customer party` IS A Party, `for a supply of goods, services or land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a small business contract` IF
    `for a supply of goods, services or land` AND (`the party is small for s 23(4)` `the supplier party` OR `the party is small for s 23(4)` `the customer party`)

GIVEN `the customer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `wholly or predominantly for personal use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a consumer contract` IF
    `the customer is an individual` AND `wholly or predominantly for personal use`

DECLARE `Contested term` HAS
    `causes a significant imbalance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the advantaged party proves it reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would cause detriment if relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defines the main subject matter, sets the upfront price or is required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is alleged to be standard form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party proves it is not standard form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded by s 28, s 28A or s 131A(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the clause` IS A `Contested term`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is unfair` IF
        `the clause`'s `causes a significant imbalance`
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `the advantaged party proves it reasonably necessary`)
    AND `the clause`'s `would cause detriment if relied on`

GIVEN `the clause` IS A `Contested term`, `the contract is a consumer or small business contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is void under s 23` IF
        `the contract is a consumer or small business contract`
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `excluded by s 28, s 28A or s 131A(2)(b)`)
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `defines the main subject matter, sets the upfront price or is required by law`)
    AND `the term is unfair` `the clause`
    AND `the clause`'s `the contract is alleged to be standard form`
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `the other party proves it is not standard form`)

GIVEN `the clause` IS A `Contested term`, `the contract is a consumer or small business contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person proposed the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proposing it contravenes s 23(2A)` IF
    `the term is void under s 23` `the clause` `the contract is a consumer or small business contract` AND `the person proposed the term`

§§ `Sch 2 s 18 -- misleading or deceptive conduct`

-- s 18(1): "A person must not, in trade or commerce, engage in conduct that is misleading or deceptive or is likely to mislead
-- or deceive." s 2: trade or commerce "includes any business or professional activity (whether or not carried on for profit)".
-- s 131A(2)(a): Part 2-1 does not apply as Commonwealth law to conduct "in relation to financial services".
-- The information-provider exception (s 19) is not modelled.
GIVEN `in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN, `misleading or deceptive or likely to be` IS A BOOLEAN, `the actor is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `in relation to financial services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct contravenes s 18` IF
        `the Schedule applies as Commonwealth law` `the actor is a corporation` `in relation to financial services`
    AND `in trade or commerce`
    AND `misleading or deceptive or likely to be`

§§ `Sch 2 s 50 -- harassment and coercion`

-- s 50(1): "A person must not use physical force, or undue harassment or coercion, in connection with: (a) the supply or possible
-- supply of goods or services; or (b) the payment for goods or services; or (c) the sale or grant ... of an interest in land; or
-- (d) the payment for an interest in land." A pecuniary penalty may be imposed.
-- s 131A(1): the Division applying the Schedule as Commonwealth law "does not apply ... to the supply ... of services that are
-- financial services, or of financial products" -- a credit card debt is collected under the ASIC Act instead (an inference;
-- the ASIC Act is not deposited here).
GIVEN `the collector is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the debt arises from financial services or products` IS A BOOLEAN, `connected with payment for goods, services or land` IS A BOOLEAN, `physical force, undue harassment or coercion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the collector contravenes s 50` IF
        `the Schedule applies as Commonwealth law` `the collector is a corporation` `the debt arises from financial services or products`
    AND `connected with payment for goods, services or land`
    AND `physical force, undue harassment or coercion`

§§ `Part IVA -- when an acquisition must be notified to the ACCC`

-- s 51ABB(1): the acquisitions provisions apply to "(a) an acquisition by a corporation of shares in the capital of a body
-- corporate; (b) an acquisition by a corporation of any assets of a person" and acquisitions of shares in or assets of a
-- corporation. s 51ABD(1): not to "a restructure or reorganisation of a group of persons who are related" bodies corporate.
-- s 51ABO: "an acquisition is required to be notified if: (a) the acquisition is put into effect on or after 1 January 2026; and
-- (b) the acquisition: (i) occurs in circumstances determined under subsection 51ABP(1) ...; or (ii) is in a class of
-- acquisitions determined under subsection 51ABQ(1) ...; and (c) the acquisition: (i) does not occur in circumstances
-- determined under subsection 51ABRA(1) ...; and (ii) is not in a class ... determined under subsection 51ABRB(1)".
-- s 51ABP(1), (2): "The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine circumstances" which "must be determined wholly or
-- partly by reference to the acquisition meeting a specified threshold" -- of value, turnover, market concentration or assets
-- (3). THE THRESHOLDS ARE NOT IN THE ACT: an INPUT.
-- s 51ABS(1): a share acquisition "is not required to be notified if: (a) immediately after ... the person does not control
-- ... the body corporate; or (b) the person controlled the body corporate immediately before", unless (5) it is in a class the
-- Minister determines under (6).
-- s 51ABT(1): shares in a Chapter 6 entity need no notice unless someone's voting power rises from 20% or below to above 20%,
-- or from above 20% (and below 100%). s 51ABJ(1): a Chapter 6 entity is "(a) a listed company ...; or (b) an unlisted company
-- with more than 50 members ...; or (c) a listed registered scheme".
-- s 51ABV(6): if the ACCC grants a waiver, "the acquisition is not required to be notified".
-- s 51ABE(1), (2): an acquisition that "is required to be notified; but ... is not a notified acquisition" "is stayed".
GIVEN `listed` IS A BOOLEAN, `members` IS A NUMBER, `a listed registered scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a Chapter 6 entity` IF
    `listed` OR `members` GREATER THAN 50 OR `a listed registered scheme`

DECLARE `Proposed acquisition` HAS
    `the acquisitions provisions apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an internal restructure of related bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `put into effect on` IS A NUMBER
    `meets a threshold the Minister has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a class the Minister has determined notifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in circumstances or a class the Minister has exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acquirer controls the target afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acquirer controlled the target before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a class the Minister determined under s 51ABS(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the target is a Chapter 6 entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `someone's voting power crosses or rises above 20 per cent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ACCC has granted a waiver` IS A BOOLEAN

`the start of mandatory notification` MEANS 20260101

GIVEN `the deal` IS A `Proposed acquisition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the control exception applies` IF
        `the deal`'s `of shares`
    AND ((NOT `the deal`'s `the acquirer controls the target afterwards`) OR `the deal`'s `the acquirer controlled the target before`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `in a class the Minister determined under s 51ABS(6)`)

GIVEN `the deal` IS A `Proposed acquisition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acquisition must be notified` IF
        `the deal`'s `the acquisitions provisions apply to it`
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `an internal restructure of related bodies corporate`)
    AND `the deal`'s `put into effect on` AT LEAST `the start of mandatory notification`
    AND (`the deal`'s `meets a threshold the Minister has determined` OR `the deal`'s `in a class the Minister has determined notifiable`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `in circumstances or a class the Minister has exempted`)
    AND (NOT `the control exception applies` `the deal`)
    AND (NOT (`the deal`'s `of shares` AND `the deal`'s `the target is a Chapter 6 entity` AND (NOT `the deal`'s `someone's voting power crosses or rises above 20 per cent`)))
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `the ACCC has granted a waiver`)

GIVEN `the deal` IS A `Proposed acquisition`, `it has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acquisition is stayed for want of notice` IF
    `the acquisition must be notified` `the deal` AND (NOT `it has been notified`)
